  "notes": "{苦|くる}しむ means to suffer, struggle, or be in distress—physically or mentally.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive verb (no object taken).\n\nCONJUGATION (godan む-verb):\n- {苦|くる}しまない (negative)\n- {苦|くる}しみます (polite)\n- {苦|くる}しんだ (past)\n- {苦|くる}しんで (te-form)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- X⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{苦|くる}しむ: to suffer from X\n- X⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{苦|くる}しむ: to suffer due to X\n- ⟦{病気|びょうき}→病気：00771_byouki⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{苦|くる}しむ: to suffer from illness\n- ⟦{借金|しゃっきん}→借金：03203_shakkin⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{苦|くる}しむ: to struggle with debt\n- ⟦{貧困|ひんこん}→貧困：04836_hinkon⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{苦|くる}しむ: to suffer from poverty\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{苦|くる}しい→苦しい：02636_kurushii⟧: painful, difficult, agonizing\n- ⟦{苦|くる}しみ→苦しみ：14120_kurushimi⟧: suffering, pain, agony (noun)\n- ⟦{苦労|くろう}する→苦労する：25357_kurousuru⟧: to have a hard time, struggle\n- ⟦{悩|なや}む→悩む：02380_nayamu⟧: to worry, be troubled\n\nUSAGE:\n{苦|くる}しむ emphasizes ongoing suffering or distress, while ⟦{悩|なや}む→悩む：02380_nayamu⟧ focuses more on mental worry or concern.",
